dead code
- song-view-manager.js setupCapoSelector() is never called (setlist-app has its own; the
  library has no capo picker). It also sets capoSelector.key, which isn't a property
  (referenceKey is). Remove it, after checking the rest of song-view-manager for the same

styles
- css/style.css has many rules for elements that now live inside components' shadow
  DOM, where page CSS can't reach (.nav-menu-item, .key-selector, .expand-toggle, ...).
  Remove them, checking each against the light DOM pages and the two light-DOM
  components (chord-display, setlist-overview)

preferences
  - custom section visibility defaults
  - revisit the configuration panels (Preferences, Storage, media player settings): too
    much variety in layout and controls. Settings rows, switches vs checkboxes, toggle
    buttons vs radios, button sizes all differ; headings repeat ("Appearance" twice,
    "Media Player Settings" twice). Settle on one settings row pattern in shared-styles.js
    Decided: on/off settings use checkboxes, not pill-shaped toggle switches (pills are
    poor UX), sized for touch (a large box and a big tap target on the whole row).

storage/sync
- db.js and organisation-db.js reject failed writes with tx.error (14 places), which is
  still null while a request's error is reported: a failure becomes a bare null
  rejection. Reject with the request's error, as organisation-db's createOrganisation now does
- setlist-app.js and create-setlist.js still report save/add/delete failures with alert():
  give pages a non-blocking message (toast) instead. (The bookmarklet's alerts stay: they
  show on SongSelect, where Chordless has no UI.)
- storage page with no organisations says "Create your first organisation" but shows no
  Create button (select-organisation's empty state)
- edit chordpro/variants
- background syncing (periodic, and fallbacks)
- conflict resolution (currently Drive wins when edited on two devices)
- delete setlists (owner only, trashed in Drive on sync, removed on other devices):
  designed in SYNC_ARCHITECTURE.md, not built
- immediate background sync of just the changed record (setlist/song), in the
  service worker, with full sync as the backstop: designed in SYNC_ARCHITECTURE.md,
  not built. Later: durable offline write queue.
- production deployment: point chordless.app at the worker (currently a static Pages deploy)
  then test song import on real devices: file import and paste on Android and iPad, the
  bookmarklet on Android Chrome, and whether the phone/tablet tip shows on the bookmarklet page
- user-facing Drive health check / cleanup (idea): turn public/dev/drive-audit.html into an
  app feature that finds duplicate or empty setlists and stray organisation folders, and
  moves them to the Drive trash after confirmation. Would need songs covered too.

