sharing
- share links: one setlist with its charts, encrypted in the org's Drive, key in the
  link, updated in place, expiring 2 weeks after the setlist date, read-only and
  isolated on the recipient's device, QR code for in-room sharing. Designed in
  SHARING.md Part 2, not built; verify the Drive questions listed there first.
  Then remove the worker's /api/share endpoints and the SETLISTS KV binding.
- email media team
- invite people to an organisation: a dialog to share the org's Drive folder with an
  email address, as read (musicians) or write (leaders) access. The leader dropdown
  already lists the folder's members (cached at sync).
- shared users' devices can't find the org folder yet: the app only has the drive.file
  scope, which only covers files the app created for that user. Needs the Google Picker
  (user picks the folder once) or a wider scope. See SHARING.md and the worker's
  /session/invite endpoint.
- restrict editing others' setlists, using the setlist's ownerId (leader's Google email)

player
 - fix or remove "Built-in Pads": it has never worked. It loads
   /pads/<key> - WARM - CHURCHFRONT PADS.mp3 (pad-audio-controller.js), and there is no
   public/pads, so every request 404s. Those pads are copyrighted like the songs, so
   they can't be shipped with the app: users upload pad sets they own. Ideas tried: a
   Web Audio synthesiser, but everything sounded awful. Removing it means: no default
   pad set, pads off until one is uploaded, and the pickers say so.
 - keep cached pads in their own Storage Bucket (navigator.storageBuckets, Chromium
   only), marked expendable, so the browser can evict pads without the setlists and
   songs. Pads re-download from Drive. Fall back to the default caches elsewhere.
 - click stuttering start
 - survive pageloads? -maybe migrate to SPA

UI
- autoscaling font
- install nag ("install to keep your data on this device"): Safari (iOS, and macOS)
  clears a site's storage after 7 days without a visit unless it's installed,
  including the sign-in, the org's Drive folder link, unsynced changes, settings and
  pads. Show it on the home page only (never during a setlist), with "Not now" hiding
  it for a while. Chromium: an Install button via beforeinstallprompt. iOS: Share ›
  Add to Home Screen instructions (no API). Mac Safari: File › Add to Dock. Skip when
  already installed (display-mode: standalone / navigator.standalone). On iOS and Mac
  Safari the installed app has its own storage, separate from Safari's, so the user
  must sign in again there; say so in the instructions. Installing also lets Chrome
  grant persistent storage.

